# The `tabula::payload-hoist` fixture: one field in three states.
#
# Sized so the lint under test is the ONLY finding. No dead row or column,
# 4 of 12 cells IGNORE (33%, well under IGNORE_HEAVY_PERCENT), no UNREACHABLE,
# and HANDLE cells present so the matrix is not fully static -- which keeps
# `no-static-entry` out of the way without having to reason about reachability.
#
# `attempt` lives in Connecting, Backoff and Reconnecting; Live carries
# nothing. Three states is PAYLOAD_HOIST_STATES exactly, so the fixture sits on
# the boundary on purpose: an implementation using `>` instead of `>=` fails.
#
# Payloads are NOT declared here. They come from each language's adapter --
# see `spec/conformance/README.md` -- because the matrix file is the matrix,
# the same separation generated code makes between TABLE and PAYLOADS.

machine Conn
initial Connecting
states  Connecting Backoff Reconnecting Live
actions Open Fail Timeout

Connecting   | HANDLE | GO(Backoff)      | GO(Backoff)
Backoff      | IGNORE | IGNORE           | HANDLE
Reconnecting | HANDLE | GO(Backoff)      | GO(Backoff)
Live         | IGNORE | GO(Reconnecting) | IGNORE
